copy [SimTalk] - lists
Copies the entire list/table designated by <Path> and returns it as a value of data type list/table.
Remarks
The method copy(Range) copies the specified range.
If you do not specify a range, Plant Simulation copies the entire list. A range may only encompass a single
range.
If you would also like to copy the column index and/or the row index during the copy process, then enter
the column 0 and/or the row 0 into the range.
The method applies to the objects DataStack, DataQueue, DataList, DataTable, and TimeSequence.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.copy  → list or table
<Path>.copy(Range:listrange) → list or table
Parameter
The parameter Range of data type listrange designates the range.
You can then process the copied region in a number of ways:
• Assign the copied range to a local variable of the corresponding type.
Example
var MyDataList : list[integer]
MyDataList := MyDataList1.copy({1}..{5})
...
• Insert the copied range into the column of a table. The column where you paste the range has to have
the same data type as the DataList.
Example
MyDataTable.insertList(3,1,MyDataList.copy({1}..{5}))
copy [SimTalk] - lists
Plant Simulation Help 11-3963
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Make the copied range a DataList of its own. Data type is list. Therefore you can assign it to a cell in a
DataList of data type list.
Example
MyDataList.insertList(2,tab.copy({1,1}..{1,5}))
Return Value
The return value has the data type list/table.
See also
Copy [context menu, lists]
Specifying a Range of Cells [several columns] > Column Index Belongs to Contents
copy [SimTalk] - lists
