countMatches [SimTalk]
Counts how often the designated value occurs in the designated range of the list or table designated by
<Path>.
Remarks
The method applies to the objects DataStack, DataQueue, DataList, DataTable, and TimeSequence.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.countMatches(Value:any[, Range:any, CaseSensitive:boolean:=false])  
→ integer
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Value of data type any designates the value for which the matching values are counted.
• The optional parameter Range of data type any designates the range within which the method looks
for matching values. If you do not specify a range, Plant Simulation searches the entire range, i.e., the
entire range {1,1}..{*,*}.
• The optional parameter CaseSensitive of data type boolean sets if the search is case-sensitive (true) or
not (false). If you do not specify this parameter, the search is not case-sensitive.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is false.
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
Example
print MyDataTable.countMatches("a1", {1,1}..{3,12})
countMatches [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-3965
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

delete [SimTalk] - lists
Deletes the contents of the list object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The method delete(Range) deletes the specified range of the list object.
The method applies to the objects DataStack, DataQueue, DataList, DataTable, and TimeSequence.
Note
You can also delete sub-tables, which inherit their contents, with the method delete. The inheritance
relation causes the reference to be passed to the origin, thus deleting the contents in the origin.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.delete
<Path>.delete([Range:listrange, ...])
Parameter
The optional parameter Range of data type listrange designates the range which you want to delete. You
can also enter several ranges.
If you do not enter a parameter, i.e. no range, Plant Simulation deletes the contents of all cells without
the cells of the column or row index. Therefore specifying no range, corresponds to specifying the range
{1,1}..{*,*}.
If you want to delete the user-defined row index or column index of DataTables, you have to do so
explicitly by entering row 0 or column 0 respectively within the range you specify.
Example
MyDataStack.delete                                // deletes the data range
MyDataQueue.delete({2}..{4})
MyDataList.delete({1}..{5}, {8})
MyDataTable.delete({2,2}..{*,*})
MyDataTable.delete({0,1}..{0,*})                  // deletes the row index
MyDataTable.delete({"ColumnB",0}..{"ColumnB",*})  // deletes the column 
index
delete [SimTalk] - lists
11-3966 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

