openDialog [SimTalk] - lists
Opens the window of the list/table designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The method applies to the objects DataStack, DataQueue, DataList, DataTable, and TimeSequence, as well
as to sub-tables and to user-defined attribute of data type table.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.openDialog([CallOpenControl:boolean:=false]) → boolean
Parameter
The optional parameter CallOpenControl of data type boolean sets if the Open Control will be executed
(true) or not (false).
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is false.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
MyDataTable.openDialog
MyDataStack.openDialog(true)
SimTalk
closeDialog [SimTalk] - lists
openDialogBox [SimTalk]
See also
Open Object [context menu, lists]
openDialog [SimTalk] - lists
